   "date": "2017-08-01T20:55:00Z",
   "subject": "How can I Append a List with Action Button?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>I want to create a list object, lets call it X_List, that gets appended every time a particular actionButton is pressed but I also want to put an upper limit on the number of elements that can be stored in X_List by deleting the oldest element whenever necessary to make room. </div><div><br></div><div>The values stored in each element of X_List will be lists, lets call them i_list, and their components will be: </div><div>- non-reactive versions of a few reactive variables</div><div>- a data.frame that should only get created when the actionButton is pressed.</div><div><br></div><div>I have no trouble creating i_list with the following code:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">G_Set </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    set_name </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$GeneSetName<br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Hugo</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rownames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">AggGenes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Entrez</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gene_lookup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gene_lookup$Gene </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Hugo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Entrez&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    G </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Name&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> set_name</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Hugo&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Hugo</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Entrez&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Entrez</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  i_list </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> eventReactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$SaveGeneSet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    fpkm_dat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fpkm_dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Retrieve gene list from G_Set()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    genelist </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> G_Set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$Entrez<br>    genelist </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">genelist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Run GSVA </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    scores </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gsva</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fpkm_dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">genelist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">method</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ssgsea&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnaseq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    out_dat </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> G_Set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    out_dat$GSVA </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scores<br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">out_dat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m thinking I probably need to do one of the following:</div><div>- make X_List another eventReactive() object that is dependent on input$SaveGeneSet </div><div>- make X_List a reactiveValues() object and use observeEvent() to append it with an if statement to control its size</div><div>- make X_List a static environment variable and update it using observeEvent() <br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>But I haven&#39;t been able to make any of these strategies work so I&#39;m wondering if I&#39;m just approaching this the wrong way. </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
